            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for to rescue, then the Telugu for to run for it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: అప్పటికే",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అప్పటికే — appaṭikē — \"already by then\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పోలీసులు వచ్చారు, కానీ దొంగ అప్పటికే పారిపోయాడు. pōlīsulu vaccāru, kānī doṅga appaṭikē pāripōyāḍu. The police came, but the thief had already run away."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అప్పటికి, by then, with -ఏ, the ending that stresses. Compare ఇప్పటికే, already by now."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అప్పటికే (appaṭikē) is native Telugu: appaṭiki, \"by then\", from appuḍu, \"at that time\" (DEDR 4559), with the stressing ending -ē."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
