        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: అంతలో",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అంతలో — antalō — \"in the meantime\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నేను ఫోను చేశాను, అంతలో అతనే వచ్చాడు. nēnu phōnu cēśānu, antalō atanē vaccāḍu. I phoned, and in the meantime he came himself."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అంత, that much, with -లో, in: within that span. It joins two happenings that overlap."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అంతలో (antalō) is native Telugu: anta, \"that much\", from the far demonstrative a- (DEDR 1), with the locative ending -lō, \"in\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
